  <content>
<procedure>
<preliminaryRqmts>
<reqCondGroup>
<reqCondNoRef><reqCond>The hydraulic power unit is stopped and electrically isolated.</reqCond></reqCondNoRef>
</reqCondGroup>
<reqSupportEquips><supportEquipDescrGroup>
<supportEquipDescr id="seq-0001"><name>Container, oil, 5 L minimum</name><toolRef toolNumber="OIL-CONTAINER-5L"/><reqQuantity>1</reqQuantity></supportEquipDescr>
</supportEquipDescrGroup></reqSupportEquips>
<reqSupplies><supplyDescrGroup><supplyDescr id="sup-0001"><name>Lint-free cloth</name><supplyRef supplyNumber="LINT-FREE-CLOTH" supplyNumberType="sp05"/><reqQuantity>As required</reqQuantity></supplyDescr></supplyDescrGroup></reqSupplies>
<reqSpares><noSpares/></reqSpares>
<reqSafety><safetyRqmts>
<warning><warningAndCautionPara>Hydraulic oil can be hot. Let the unit become cool to less than 40 °C before you start this procedure. Hot oil can cause burns.</warningAndCautionPara></warning>
<warning><warningAndCautionPara>Make sure that the system pressure is 0 bar. Oil under pressure can cause serious injury.</warningAndCautionPara></warning>
<caution><warningAndCautionPara>Do not let dirt into the filter housing. Dirt in the hydraulic oil can cause damage to the pump and the valves.</warningAndCautionPara></caution>
</safetyRqmts></reqSafety>
</preliminaryRqmts>
<mainProcedure>
<proceduralStep><para>Make sure that the pressure gauge on the manifold shows 0 bar.</para></proceduralStep>
<proceduralStep><para>Clean the filter cover and the area around it with a lint-free cloth.</para></proceduralStep>
<proceduralStep><para>Put lint-free cloths around the filter housing to catch drops of oil.</para></proceduralStep>
<proceduralStep><para>Turn the filter cover counterclockwise and remove it.</para></proceduralStep>
<proceduralStep><para>Pull the filter element up out of the housing slowly. Let the oil drain from the element into the housing.</para></proceduralStep>
<proceduralStep><para>Put the filter element in the oil container.</para></proceduralStep>
<proceduralStep><para>Examine the inner side of the filter housing for metal particles. If you find metal particles, stop and tell your supervisor. Metal particles can show wear in the pump.</para></proceduralStep>
<proceduralStep><para>Discard the filter element in accordance with local regulations.</para></proceduralStep>
</mainProcedure>
<closeRqmts><reqCondGroup>
<reqCondDm><reqCond>Install a new filter element.</reqCond><dmRef><dmRefIdent><dmCode modelIdentCode="VH15" systemDiffCode="A" systemCode="40" subSystemCode="0" subSubSystemCode="0" assyCode="00" disassyCode="02" disassyCodeVariant="A" infoCode="720" infoCodeVariant="A" itemLocationCode="A"/></dmRefIdent></dmRef></reqCondDm>
</reqCondGroup></closeRqmts>
</procedure>
